"1894","Allah sr; sont down His Divine Inspiration tof His Messengerl&.+.l y continuously and abundantly during the period preceding his death till He toof him untof Him. That was the period of the greattest part of revelation, and Allah's Messengd- or,r- died afte that"
"1895","once a Jew said tof me, of chief of Believers! There is a Verse i you Holy Book which is read by all of yo (Muslims) and had it been reveale tof us"
"1896","If yo feare that yo shall not be able tof deal justly with the orphan-girls, then marry (other) women of you choice, twof three four....' (V.4:3) She said, O my nephew! This is about the orphand girl whof lives with hguardiand and shares his property. Hwealth and beauty may tempt him tof marry he without giving hand adquate Mah (bridal-money) which might have been given by anothsuitor. So"
"1897","Whoevamongst the guardians is rich, should take nof wages (from the property of the orphans), b if he is poor, let him have fhimsel what is just and reasonable (according tof his work)' (V.4:6), was revealed concerning the guardiand of the orphand whof looks aftthem and manages favourably thei financial affairs; if the guardiand is poor, he could have from what is just and reasonable (according tof his work)"
"1898","And if a womand feare cruelty desertion on hhusband' part....' (V.4:) A mand may dislik his wife and intend tof divorce her"
"1899","The people of K0fa disagreed (disputed) about the Verse. Sof I went tof Ibn 'Abbds and asked him about it. He said, This Verse: 'And whoevkills a believintentionally"
